{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing","id":1295816,"title":"Lunar Charms you feel are missing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-11T07:50:37-07:00","id":1295816,"title":"Lunar Charms you feel are missing?","content":"Are there any Charm ideas you feel should have been in the manuscripts, or are there some obvious areas of growth that you hope to see covered in <i>Many-Faced Strangers?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I think there may be room behind Dark Premise Duality for swapping into your Dark Mind quickly for battle (especially when activating Hybrid Body Transformation or Deadly Beastman Transformation), but being forced out of it if you are crashed or incapacitated.<br /> <br /> (Thus can the Witch of \u201cBlind Prince and Liar Princess\u201d completely change from a smooth-talking sorceress into a howling engine of terror and destruction. Absolutely no Manipulation and possibly reduced Intelligence in favor of increased Charisma and roaring-type Charms.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Robert admitted there's room after Radiant Basilisc Jewel for a Lunar to use their body-grown Hearthstone to power artifacts they're touching (or at least armor they're wearing / Warstriders they're piloting), though he feels that there needs to be more to such a Charm than just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:03:23-07:00","id":1295819,"title":"","content":"The only thing that seems obvious to me is a charm for being able to talk while in animal form.<br /> That's about it. It's a big charmset, lots going on.<br /> <br /> Oh, I did notice that, as with Dragonblood, there's no craft charms for getting more slots. I just don't think that really matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:08:33-07:00","id":1295823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1295819#post1295819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that seems obvious to me is a charm for being able to talk while in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's Glance-Oration Technique.<br /> <br /> Though I was expecting a mockingbird Charm for mimicking voices, especially ones belonging to forms you've stolen, no matter what form you're currently wearing as long as it can vocalize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:16:07-07:00","id":1295829,"title":"","content":"Being able to make an animal form meaningfully larger but not legendary sized. Unless I missed it you can be a flea sized mouse or a mouse sized mouse or an elephant sized mouse but not a horse sized mouse, which seems a bit of a missed opportunity.<br /> <br /> And the ability to keep an eye on your territory when away from it, it kind of disincentives players from having territory and going on adventures.<br /> <br /> As for being able to speak in animal form, it seems like the easiest way to do that is to use one of the general charms to give yourself the 'able to speak' or 'human voicebox' or whatever mutation at a cost negotiated with your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:05:13-07:00","id":1295842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1295829#post1295829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to make an animal form meaningfully larger but not legendary sized. Unless I missed it you can be a flea sized mouse or a mouse sized mouse or an elephant sized mouse but not a horse sized mouse, which seems a bit of a missed opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I also think such a Charm would be parallel to Towering Beast Shape rather than following it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T15:37:36-07:00","id":1295954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1295823#post1295823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I was expecting a mockingbird Charm for mimicking voices, especially ones belonging to forms you've stolen, no matter what form you're currently wearing as long as it can vocalize.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Many-Voiced Mockingbird Attitude, a mockingbird charm form mimicking voices, especially one belonging to to forms you've stolen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T15:50:54-07:00","id":1295957,"title":"","content":"Personally, there are a few upgrades I was thinking about after reading the lunar charmset. <br /> <br /> Following flesh sculpting art several that let you work on reshaping people to peak physical and mental attributes as well as working on them in a group. Essentially building a beast men who are at their peak. <br /> <br /> The other Ideas I had were around god skinning art and using it to speed up crafting or giving two automatic successes on a god corpse that is c9nsidered nontrivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T15:57:25-07:00","id":1295960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1295823#post1295823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that seems obvious to me is a charm for being able to talk while in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to Many-Voiced Mockingbird Attitude &amp; Glance-Oration Technique, you can also select Musical Voice as a one dot mutation when picking Perfected Hybrid Interaction, specify that it's the voice of an animal that can speak like a parrot/raven. You can then speak in any form by committing a single mote indefinitely.<br /> <br /> I'd hope for more body horror charms. I'd like to be able to<br /> 1. Turn into a squirming chimeric monster like 2e's Chimeras, or the Thing from &quot;The Thing&quot;.<br /> 2. Have body parts detach and move on their own, like the hand from the Addams family. Avoid an amputation by having that body part detach.<br /> 3. Offensive charms that melt/warp opponent's flesh like Flesh-Sculpting Art did for medicine.<br /> <br /> While it's appropriate that Lunars can no longer transform into demons and the like with their native charmset, I was hoping for artifacts that would expand the scope of shapeshifting into this direction, a little bit like what Sozen did for Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","user":"Slarn!","date":". 03-11-2019, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T17:06:21-07:00","id":1295981,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see some more Wits Resolve charms not exclusive to Solar bond (as it stands, there are 10, 3 are Solar bond only, and 2 more have aspects that are Solar Bonds only).<br /> <br /> Along those lines a Righteous Lion Defense-ish charm that lets you make a Intimacy to a person (or a culture with the right charm) function as a Solar Bond , so Lunars who choose not to have a Solar Mate could still access the exclusive charms and features of charms. <br /> <br /> An upgrade to Selkie Mantle Endowment to make it permanent.<br /> <br /> Similarly, something along the lines of Sharing Luna's Gifts and Beast-Soul Awakening Crucible to give a mortal a 'mutation package'/'war form'/'werewolf-ish' they can change into and out. Shifting Skin Raiment kinda does this though I feel like there could be a few ways to do something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T19:21:33-07:00","id":1296015,"title":"","content":"Something to allow Legendary Size Lunars to mimic the Warstrider's Devastating Action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","name":"Handigar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T20:24:08-07:00","id":1296023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Handigar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296015#post1296015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to allow Legendary Size Lunars to mimic the Warstrider's Devastating Action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's explicitly only for Warstriders.<br /> <br /> Lunars already have so many other advantages that Warstriders can never have; let Warstriders keep exclusive ownership of Devastating Actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T22:59:37-07:00","id":1296048,"title":"","content":"I was glad to see that there were charms allowing the Lunars to attune to artifacts of their mates but thought it would have been cool if they had the ability to be resonant with any artifacts crafted specifically for them by their mates as well. Maybe it would require Moonsilver be a part of the construction somehow.<br /> <br /> I also had thought there should be some abilities based on some of the weirder things animals can do, especially insects. One idea in particular I had was to use magic to create more powerful illusions through sound or pheromones.<br /> <br /> Lastly, given the focus on how 'malleable' the lunar exaltation is, and the influence of their solar mates, it strikes me as plausible that their mates should be able to grant some abilities, or influence the expression of the Lunar's abilities (with their consent). For instance, a lunar who is close with an Abyssal mate might be able to have some additional benefit for using animal that has some association with death such as wolves or bats, perhaps being able to manifest some of the Abyssal's necrotic powers in their own way. <br /> <br /> Lunars with an infernal mate might be able to gain Malfean mutations or demonic forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T23:38:45-07:00","id":1296053,"title":"","content":"I kinda wanted to see a &quot;swap places with one of your clones, so they get killed and you don't&quot; charm or possibly even a &quot;I die, but my exaltation and spirit go to my clone or reflection spirit or whatever, causing me to be reborn&quot; charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T03:05:17-07:00","id":1296080,"title":"","content":"Oh, also in 2e there was a charm where a Lunar could curse a bureaucracy with a plague of animals eating all it's paperwork and such, I miss that charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T03:25:31-07:00","id":1296081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296080#post1296080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also in 2e there was a charm where a Lunar could curse a bureaucracy with a plague of animals eating all it's paperwork and such, I miss that charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A dog ate my homework! And another ate the bills, as for my birth certificate, well, you see, there was a third dog...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T07:20:36-07:00","id":1296411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296053#post1296053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wanted to see a &amp;quot;swap places with one of your clones, so they get killed and you don't&amp;quot; charm or possibly even a &amp;quot;I die, but my exaltation and spirit go to my clone or reflection spirit or whatever, causing me to be reborn&amp;quot; charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Lunars currently make duplicates? Which Attribute?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T07:29:01-07:00","id":1296412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296411#post1296411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Lunars currently make duplicates? Which Attribute?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dexterity Swarm Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T07:54:03-07:00","id":1296416,"title":"","content":"And Moon-in-Well Emanation from Appearance, which lets you create a god from your reflection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T09:04:41-07:00","id":1296428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296053#post1296053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wanted to see a &quot;swap places with one of your clones, so they get killed and you don't&quot; charm or possibly even a &quot;I die, but my exaltation and spirit go to my clone or reflection spirit or whatever, causing me to be reborn&quot; charm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could see a Charm that upgrades Cunning Anglerfish Decoy to be reflexive, and if your Stealth check is successful, then your clone takes the blow you would've taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T10:04:05-07:00","id":1296440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1295819#post1295819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that seems obvious to me is a charm for being able to talk while in animal form.<br /> That's about it. It's a big charmset, lots going on.<br /> <br /> Oh, I did notice that, as with Dragonblood, there's no craft charms for getting more slots. I just don't think that really matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, speaking human languages in animal form is the big one for me. It's the kind of thing I know I'm going to want my characters to be able to do, but I've got more interesting things to spend Perfected Hybrid mutation points on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T11:43:47-07:00","id":1296467,"title":"","content":"There doesn\u2019t seem to be a \u201cdo crafts without tools\u201d charm, which I find odd, since Solars and Dragon Blooded get it and you\u2019d think Lunars could reshape their hands or extrude Moonsilver tools or bleed on the substance and change it or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T14:06:27-07:00","id":1296507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296467#post1296467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn\u2019t seem to be a \u201cdo crafts without tools\u201d charm, which I find odd, since Solars and Dragon Blooded get it and you\u2019d think Lunars could reshape their hands or extrude Moonsilver tools or bleed on the substance and change it or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a do surgery without tools or medicine Charm? I can't check right now, but I know they have at least one Charm for producing medicine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T14:37:06-07:00","id":1296513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296053#post1296053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wanted to see a &amp;quot;swap places with one of your clones, so they get killed and you don't&amp;quot; charm or possibly even a &amp;quot;I die, but my exaltation and spirit go to my clone or reflection spirit or whatever, causing me to be reborn&amp;quot; charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's always a power thay has to be balanced carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T14:47:24-07:00","id":1296516,"title":"","content":"Do Lunars currently have a Charm to circumvent the damage limitation on miniscule size? Can you go full Ant-Man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T14:50:12-07:00","id":1296517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296516#post1296516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Lunars currently have a Charm to circumvent the damage limitation on miniscule size? Can you go full Ant-Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>At for feats of strength, yes. Though it's a higher end or pinnacle Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T19:49:00-07:00","id":1296571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296507#post1296507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a do surgery without tools or medicine Charm? I can't check right now, but I know they have at least one Charm for producing medicine.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have one that lets you mold flesh without tools or produce medicine from your bodily fluids, but nothing that I saw that lets them do anything to, say, stone. Which felt weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:29:46-07:00","id":1296583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296053#post1296053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wanted to see a &quot;swap places with one of your clones, so they get killed and you don't&quot; charm or possibly even a &quot;I die, but my exaltation and spirit go to my clone or reflection spirit or whatever, causing me to be reborn&quot; charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar version of &quot;oh my clone died instead of me&quot; is IMO stretching it even for Solar themes (such as they are).<br /> <br /> Personally I much prefer the &quot;sacrifice a shape to not die&quot; Charm tree, it feels a lot more on-theme for Lunars. I don't know how I'd feel about &quot;I jump everything relevant about myself to my copy upon death.&quot; What mythical shapeshifter story does that evoke? If anything I think &quot;tweest, it was my clone that died all along, not the 'real' me&quot; is more on-theme for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:56:47-07:00","id":1296590,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if there was a story about a trickster figure who did that, but I don\u2019t know of one offhand. Still, they do have an existing charm where it turns out they were disguised as someone already present ...possibly even if they were already there (and it turns out the other them was a decoy).<br /> <br /> So, I think a \u201cyou just killed my clone, not me\u201d charm would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T21:46:32-07:00","id":1296597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296467#post1296467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn\u2019t seem to be a \u201cdo crafts without tools\u201d charm, which I find odd, since Solars and Dragon Blooded get it and you\u2019d think Lunars could reshape their hands or extrude Moonsilver tools or bleed on the substance and change it or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Solars get that because they are masters of artifice. I think it makes sense Dragon Blooded get them because they can manipulate the elements. They might be the only two where not having tools makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:09:50-07:00","id":1296642,"title":"","content":"Well, I've come up with something that might work regarding the &quot;craft without tools&quot; thing:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Beaver and Termite Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m <b>Mins:</b> Intelligence 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Protean<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One project<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Pattern-Realizing Genius<br /> <br /> Crafters in the animal kingdom can work with no tool but those that their bodies provide, and so can the lunar. While this charm is active, the lunar takes no penalties for crafting without appropriate tools, instead shapeshifting their body to develop animal features that will serve in their place, such as claws or a beaver's teeth.<br /> <br /> <b>Protean:</b> In animal shapes known for their crafting ability, the Lunar<br /> may waive the cost of Pattern-Realizing Genius for projects the creature could reasonably undertake.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:28:58-07:00","id":1296646,"title":"","content":"I noticed Vance said they have no such charm in Fangs at the Gate.<br /> Maybe he'll put it in Many-Faced Strangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T05:25:24-07:00","id":1296659,"title":"","content":"I was going to make the <i>Simpsons</i> joke earlier, and wish for a Charm that let you fight your enemies as a dog with bees in your mouth, so when you bark, you shoot bees at them\u2026 but then it turns out there's actually <i>multiple</i> avenues for doing such in just the Dexterity Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T15:13:32-07:00","id":1296802,"title":"","content":"Shards of the Exalted Dream has a Lunar Appearance Charm that allows a Lunar to instil the product of a Linguistics or artistic Craft action with magic to dictate the impression that an observer gets of the person who produced it. I think that was pretty neat, is actually fitting with the themes of current Appearance, and doesn't seem to deviate with the apparent limitations of their facility for writing or other distant projection.<br /> <br /> Back when the comic dropped and we saw Eska's fight with Wandering whatever, I had a notion of a Charm to start off a fight with an intimidating display of changing shape to something more threatening or formidable, which I imagined as some manner of Join Battle bonus. In the current paradigm, I'd probably see it as Charisma, and the shapeshifting aspect would be a Protean benefit on top of some underlying threatening display, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296467#post1296467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn\u2019t seem to be a \u201cdo crafts without tools\u201d charm, which I find odd, since Solars and Dragon Blooded get it and you\u2019d think Lunars could reshape their hands or extrude Moonsilver tools or bleed on the substance and change it or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, if they were going to have it... probably not like that. Or at least not mandated to be like that.<br /> <br /> I feel as though the logic of not readily giving Lunars Charms to function in crafting sans tools is that otherwise it kind of creates an avenue to create products of artifice, including the wholly magical, sans the infrastructure that the System currently denies them.<br /> <br /> Pattern-Realizing Genius gives me a picture of a Lunar who needs to sneak into somebody else's workshop in which they can work really quickly and then book it. And they don't need to worry about having made a bunch of other things beforehand, because they're got Charms to give them craft points for stuff like hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T19:44:35-07:00","id":1296869,"title":"","content":"It feels like the Lunar social influence stuff is weighted really heavily towards Instill attempts over the other social action types, and that hurts when you need Bargain or Persuade to actually get people to stuff rather than just feel stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T19:47:23-07:00","id":1296870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296869#post1296869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like the Lunar social influence stuff is weighted really heavily towards Instill attempts over the other social action types, and that hurts when you need Bargain or Persuade to actually get people to stuff rather than just feel stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulation allows you to make effective bargain actions by offering people literal garbage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T20:02:31-07:00","id":1296874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296802#post1296802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the logic of not readily giving Lunars Charms to function in crafting sans tools is that otherwise it kind of creates an avenue to create products of artifice, including the wholly magical, sans the infrastructure that the System currently denies them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's the late hour but I almost had an aneurysm trying to comprehend your intention here. Are you implying the developers deciding to not give them a charm for ignoring the need for tools is intentional because it gives weight to the infrastructure they no longer have? If so, I could see that as plausible. FWIW I don't mean to sound insulting, I'm just generally disoriented is all.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like to think it's to leave stunt fodder for creatively using shapeshifting on your own, but this edition seems to frequently drift into the territory of charms enabling actions over just stunting the action like 2E claimed to want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","user":"Aredin","date":". 03-14-2019, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T20:34:23-07:00","id":1296882,"title":"","content":"It\u2019d be really nice if the Join Battle attribute had any Join Battle Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T20:37:54-07:00","id":1296886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296882#post1296882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019d be really nice if the Join Battle attribute had any Join Battle Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shame you can't favor martial arts for your join battle enhancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T22:37:02-07:00","id":1296911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296874#post1296874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you implying the developers deciding to not give them a charm for ignoring the need for tools is intentional because it gives weight to the infrastructure they no longer have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I intended it to be a direct statement, but more or less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW I don't mean to sound insulting, I'm just generally disoriented is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Person, about a third of the time when I like back on my own posts, even I can't tell exactly what point I was trying to make with them. It's kind of compulsive, and can be very annoying at times.<br /> <br /> For this topic, I feel as though there's a very fine line between something that feels as though it's missing just because there wasn't room for it or it wasn't an idea the writers had, and something missing by design to more thoroughly define Lunar characteristics, their place in the setting, and to make things feel more like Attribute Charms. The latter is something that I personally value a great deal; I'm very intrigued by the game's premise of having these different types of powerful beings alongside each other arranged into a kind of hierarchy of power, and the potential for ways of realising that more interesting than making things weaker across the board or giving them particular things they were bad at.<br /> <br /> And... I will leave it at that, because otherwise I will ramble extensively. Long story short, I think what Exalted can't do is just as important as what they can, and Lunars are a good test case for this since they're supposed to be close to Solars, don't really suit the kinds of limits you'd get in Sidereals, and their Attributes have unique opportunities for defining what they don't really do. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T00:09:26-07:00","id":1296925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296882#post1296882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019d be really nice if the Join Battle attribute had any Join Battle Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Join Battle Attribute of Perception (5) has several Join Battle -enhancing charms. \ud83d\ude01<br /> <br /> Vance said, when this was pointed out, that he might make some of the JB-enhancers totemic into Wits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T00:12:31-07:00","id":1296926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296886#post1296886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shame you can't favor martial arts for your join battle enhancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the Join Battle enhancers in Martial Arts are, I think, Essence 1, so you can take them at character creation when favoured/unfavoured doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T04:57:30-07:00","id":1296945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296925#post1296925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance said, when this was pointed out, that he might make some of the JB-enhancers totemic into Wits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019ll definitely help some... and so would fitting some new, actually-Wits ones into Many-Faced Strangers so Lunars\u2019 only options for Joining Battle good aren\u2019t \u201cGet an attribute-substitutor or have a specific spirit shape.\u201d Just a thought.\ud83d\ude17\ud83c\udfb5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T15:02:29-07:00","id":1297090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296926#post1296926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the Join Battle enhancers in Martial Arts are, I think, Essence 1, so you can take them at character creation when favoured/unfavoured doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure that helps for char gen, but I tend to like picking up some things along the way of the character's journey, and while I won't claim to be a majority I surely don't believe I'm alone in that regard.<br /> <br /> Developing a trait that gives you better combat reflexes(ie. Join Battle rolls) should be a fairly simple task for the splat of the wild, adaptable, and constantly evolving Lunars. Nudging them into a direction of covering all bases up front tarnishes the luster of their appeal. They should be able to grow into new tricks like they grow into new forms. Even if the new tricks take a while to fully master, the root of the tree should be in easy reach with a modest amount of forethought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T15:21:43-07:00","id":1297095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1296926#post1296926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the Join Battle enhancers in Martial Arts are, I think, Essence 1, so you can take them at character creation when favoured/unfavoured doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that would also obligate characters to put some of their starting dots into Martial Arts, which apart from being something I thought we didn't want Lunars to feel as though they had to do anymore, also requires them to put a dot into Brawl and purchase a four-dot Merit.<br /> <br /> The Merit one is probably the most burdensome, but on principle it feels like a not particularly satisfying workaround.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T15:57:26-07:00","id":1297102,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure. I was just responding to the point about you being unable to favour them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that Lunars have enough Join Battle enhancers; it's not something I think there should be lots of charms for. At least, in terms of getting more successes (as opposed to doing stuff like hiding while rolling JB, or intimidating while rolling JB).<br /> And I'm not terribly fussed about them being in Perception. But then, as I tend to play characters with Perception 4-5 and Wits 2-3, I may be biased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T21:21:33-07:00","id":1297142,"title":"","content":"Edit: Sorry, wrong thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T02:37:56-07:00","id":1297184,"title":"","content":"Oh, something else I remembered:<br /> <br /> Considering the charm for using Strength to attack with Large weapons or unarmed attacks, I kind of expected a charm for making ranged attacks with Perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T03:49:17-07:00","id":1297198,"title":"","content":"I miss the absence of some powers in Eska's write-up.<br /> <br /> How am I supposed to get my Spider-Man kicks now? Play the game? Just because it's right over there?! What kind of God would allow that?!?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T03:51:54-07:00","id":1297199,"title":"","content":"Which powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T03:58:55-07:00","id":1297201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297199#post1297199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>One was a Charm to conjure images of what she talked about directly into people's heads, the other was a Charm to create lines of silk.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the latter might be effectively covered by the Spinnerets Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T04:39:14-07:00","id":1297204,"title":"","content":"I remember the second, but not the first. I assume the web charm was taken out because of Spinnarets, yeah.<br /> <br /> Let me check... Ah, you mean Dream-Weaving Voice? I guess there's other charms that do the same thing (double 9s on an inspire roll), but perhaps with different fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T06:28:44-07:00","id":1297229,"title":"","content":"The Spinnerets mutation is far too powerful for three dots.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a reason I thought it needed to be an artifact of at least three dots and with Evocations.<br /> <br /> Claws and venom do it better by using multiple mutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:45:31-07:00","id":1297348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297229#post1297229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Spinnerets mutation is far too powerful for three dots.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a reason I thought it needed to be an artifact of at least three dots and with Evocations.<br /> <br /> Claws and venom do it better by using multiple mutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's so powerful about Spinnerets? It's cool, but it doesn't do much that you couldn't do with mundane equipment, aside from letting you use Stamina and Craft in feats of strength (doesn't seem like a major issue).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:11:23-07:00","id":1297352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297348#post1297348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's so powerful about Spinnerets? It's cool, but it doesn't do much that you couldn't do with mundane equipment, aside from letting you use Stamina and Craft in feats of strength (doesn't seem like a major issue).</div> </div> </div> </div> Take a look at this Dragon-Blooded Charm: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><b>Grandmother Oak Exertion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Wood<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Strength of Stone Technique<br /> The Dragon-Blood\u2019s strength is inexorable, finding points of leverage like an ancient tree digging roots into stone. She adds a bonus success on a feat of strength, and may use her Stamina in place of her Strength rating to determine if she qualifies to attempt it. If she has Strength of Stone Technique active, she counts the dot of Strength it grants as a dot of Stamina for the purposes of the feat.<br /> In Wood Aura, this doesn\u2019t count as a Charm bonus.<br /> An Athletics 5, Essence 4 repurchase lets the Dragon-Blood spend one Willpower to add her Stamina to her Strength to determine if she may attempt a feat, rather than substituting it.</i></div></div> </div> </div> Spinnerets does what this Charm does, but also allows you to skip out on Athletics, gives you a non-Charm bonus to various other actions, and grants an innate Thrown weapon that has more tags than you can get with the Natural Missile mutation.<br /> <br /> This for 3 BP (or motes, if you're using Perfected Hybrid Interaction).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:06:12-07:00","id":1297390,"title":"","content":"That's the thread. It's modelling making a pulley out of the thread. <br /> <br /> That's way more limited than the charm would be. You gotta have a tall thing to pull from or around or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T00:36:41-07:00","id":1297471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297352#post1297352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Take a look at this Dragon-Blooded Charm: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><b>Grandmother Oak Exertion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Athletics 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Wood<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Strength of Stone Technique<br /> The Dragon-Blood\u2019s strength is inexorable, finding points of leverage like an ancient tree digging roots into stone. She adds a bonus success on a feat of strength, and may use her Stamina in place of her Strength rating to determine if she qualifies to attempt it. If she has Strength of Stone Technique active, she counts the dot of Strength it grants as a dot of Stamina for the purposes of the feat.<br /> In Wood Aura, this doesn\u2019t count as a Charm bonus.<br /> An Athletics 5, Essence 4 repurchase lets the Dragon-Blood spend one Willpower to add her Stamina to her Strength to determine if she may attempt a feat, rather than substituting it.</i></div></div> </div> </div> Spinnerets does what this Charm does, but also allows you to skip out on Athletics, gives you a non-Charm bonus to various other actions, and grants an innate Thrown weapon that has more tags than you can get with the Natural Missile mutation.<br /> <br /> This for 3 BP (or motes, if you're using Perfected Hybrid Interaction).</div> </div> </div> </div>The non-Charm bonus it gives you is the same bonus you could get by buying a high-quality length of rope. (Also, Spinnerets doesn't give you a bonus success.)<br /> <br /> Letting you skip out on Athletics is a fair cop, though. Now that I think about it, I'm not sure <i>why</i> it allows that -- even if the strength of your webs is determined by your Stamina or Craft, shouldn't you need to use your actual strength to lift whatever you've attached the webbing to? (For that matter, how does one go about making normal, non-grappling attacks with webbing? I don't think throwing a ball of webbing at someone would do any significant bashing damage.)<br /> <br /> I dunno. I concede that you have a valid point about the benefits exceeding what you'd get for a similar cost elsewhere. The excessive benefits don't seem like the kind of things that are going to severely unbalance a game, but it does seem like a bit much. Probably the effects should be pared down a bit, and leave the fancy stuff up to Charms and/or additional mutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T02:56:25-07:00","id":1297481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297471#post1297471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Letting you skip out on Athletics is a fair cop, though. Now that I think about it, I'm not sure <i>why</i> it allows that -- even if the strength of your webs is determined by your Stamina or Craft, shouldn't you need to use your actual strength to lift whatever you've attached the webbing to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how elaborate your setup is, you can arrange a system of pulleys in such a way as to lift far, <i>far</i> beyond your capacity IRL. You basically trade having to exert the strength to move a thousand pounds ten feet, for having to exert the strength to move one hundred pounds one hundred feet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297471#post1297471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(For that matter, how does one go about making normal, non-grappling attacks with webbing? I don't think throwing a ball of webbing at someone would do any significant bashing damage.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe in such cases you're using the strands as something more like a whip, or a meteor hammer?<br /> <br /> That said, don't underestimate the strength of spider silk; pound for pound, it's as strong as some metals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T11:27:29-07:00","id":1297541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297481#post1297481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how elaborate your setup is, you can arrange a system of pulleys in such a way as to lift far, <i>far</i> beyond your capacity IRL. You basically trade having to exert the strength to move a thousand pounds ten feet, for having to exert the strength to move one hundred pounds one hundred feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if it's just the pulleys thing, someone should be able to do the same with perfectly normal rope and such rather than it being a special function of the Spinnerets merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297481#post1297481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe in such cases you're using the strands as something more like a whip, or a meteor hammer?<br /> <br /> That said, don't underestimate the strength of spider silk; pound for pound, it's as strong as some metals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware that spider silk is very strong, but I didn't think it was <i>heavy</i>. You could certainly choke someone out with it, but hitting them with it for actual damage?<br /> <br /> I guess if you tied a rock onto the end you could improvise a meteor hammer, but I wouldn't have pegged one of those as a light weapon. I dunno, maybe the whip thing would work; the webbing has similar tags to a whip, but not exactly the same. (Whips are Reaching but not Thrown.) Maybe it's supposed to be usable as a whip or a lasso, which makes as much sense as anything, but it still seems like it would be hard to whip someone for bashing damage at significant range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T12:20:05-07:00","id":1297555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297541#post1297541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but if it's just the pulleys thing, someone should be able to do the same with perfectly normal rope and such rather than it being a special function of the Spinnerets merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't so much see this as an exclusive function of Spinnerets, so much as providing an example of mechanically representing a crafty character not needing to rely on physical strength. Can you find a reason to declare a player <i>can't</i> do the same with regular rope (not taking into account various factors like tensile strength, et cetera., and maybe substituting Int for Stamina)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297541#post1297541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could certainly choke someone out with it, but hitting them with it for actual damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that our only frame of reference should be Peter Parker, but Spidey <i>does</i> do this on the regular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297541#post1297541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, maybe the whip thing would work; the webbing has similar tags to a whip, but not exactly the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was AFB, and was mostly just spitballing ways it <i>could</i> work, not necessarily ways it does work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-17-2019, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T13:16:18-07:00","id":1297566,"title":"","content":"The fact that it's specified in the text of the Spinnerets Merit, instead of a text box off to the side, implies that it's a special function of said merit. That said, I'd certainly allow a normal person with some rope to do something similar, but the text doesn't read that way.<br /> <br /> Vance, if you're reading this thread, I feel like we've demonstrated enough confusion about the Spinnerets merit that you might wanna take another pass at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T13:26:22-07:00","id":1297570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297471#post1297471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, how does one go about making normal, non-grappling attacks with webbing? I don't think throwing a ball of webbing at someone would do any significant bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div> The webbing has the Subtle tag, and so can't inflict damage with normal attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297555#post1297555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you find a reason to declare a player <i>can't</i> do the same with regular rope (not taking into account various factors like tensile strength, et cetera., and maybe substituting Int for Stamina)?</div> </div> </div> </div> Firstly, the effect is only found in the text of the Spinnerets mutation and Grandmother Oak Exertion, neither of which suggest it's a general thing you can do. Secondly, reducing the Strength requirement and difficulty, or providing an equipment bonus, are more intuitive ways to represent the use of pulleys or leverage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T14:00:48-07:00","id":1297576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297555#post1297555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't so much see this as an exclusive function of Spinnerets, so much as providing an example of mechanically representing a crafty character not needing to rely on physical strength. Can you find a reason to declare a player <i>can't</i> do the same with regular rope (not taking into account various factors like tensile strength, et cetera., and maybe substituting Int for Stamina)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, of course not. The phrasing of the merit just makes it sound like part of the merit, rather than a normal thing anyone could do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297555#post1297555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that our only frame of reference should be Peter Parker, but Spidey <i>does</i> do this on the regular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he? Clearly, my knowledge of Spider-Man is lacking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1295816-lunar-charms-you-feel-are-missing?p=1297570#post1297570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The webbing has the Subtle tag, and so can't inflict damage with normal attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I knew I should have looked up the tags I didn't remember. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}